 have good news  Sleeping Beauty's castle was inspired by  the neuschwanstein castle in germany  it's easy to see why walt shows this  castle as an inspiration  it looks just like a fairytale castle  already the castle was commissioned by  King Ludwig is the second in 1869 Ludwik  was known for being eccentric and  innovative he came up with many projects  but this was the most notable he wanted  a castle built on a steep rock high  above village what makes this castle  different from any of those in its time  was its bright colors the rooms in the  castle also displayed King Ludwig's  over-the-top and eccentric personality  with its fairytale location in the  Bavarian Alps in Germany it's easy to  understand why Walt Disney fell in love  with this in the first place the Little  Mermaid chateau de chillon if you've  ever wanted to be part of Ariel's world  and live in Prince Eric's castle we've  got a surprise for you how many of us  wanted to rock Ariel's pink dress  get your Dingle hoppers and gadgets  ready because we are taking you to  Prince Eric's castle yes this beautiful  castle is very much real and yes you can  visit Prince Eric's castle is based on  the chateau de chillon on the west end  of Lake Geneva in Switzerland the first  written account of this castle  dates back to the Year 1150 it was  originally used as a fort to control the  path between the lake and the mountains  it was later taken over in 1536 by the  Bernese it was used as a fortress  Arsenal in prison for 260 years the  castle then became a national property  of the canton of Vaud in 1803 the  British poet Lord Byron visited the  castle in 1816 it was inspired by the  story of one of its inmates Byron wrote  the poem The Prisoner of Chillon which  helped make the castle famous with a  view of Lake Geneva in the Alps it's no  wonder why this was the basis for Eric's  Castle frozen Hotel des glass when  disney's frozen was released in 2013 we  all saying let it go at the top of our  lungs right we can all agree that Queen  Elsa's ballad was catchy but it was her  ice dress and ice palace that took our  breath away although we aren't sure how  to explain Elsa's ice dress and cake we  know that the ice palace is a work of  art would you like to live in else's  palace well you definitely can because  the real-life inspiration for the castle  is in the Hotel des Glass in Canada the  hotel first opened in 2001 and was  founded by G drew on but what happens  when the ice melts the hotel is only  open during the winter season and the  design varies every year the hotel  boasts 44 rooms and suites along with  ice furniture sculptures chapel bar and  a Grand Hall local artists are hired to  carve designs and sculptures the hotel  even created a frozen suite inspired by  the film that was inspired by Anna and  Elsa's bedrooms back in 2014  this gorgeous Ice Hotel is almost enough  to make us surrender the Sun because the  cold never bothered us anyway The  Hunchback of Notre Dame Notre Dame  Cathedral one of the most beautifully  animated films features a beautiful  cathedral and the bellringer Quasimodo  Disney's The Hunchback of Notre DOM is  based on Victor Hugo's novel of the same  name if the name sounds a bit familiar  is because he also wrote lay miserab  which also was turned into a musical and  a film The Hunchback of Notre Dom story  takes place in Paris France mostly  around the actual Cathedral okay so we  know that this one is pretty obvious as  the location is included in the title  but we love this film because of how  true it stays to the location the  notre-dame Cathedral was home to the  deformed hero with the biggest heart and  spirit Quasimodo we can see a lot of the  Cathedral in the animated version it is  impressive how much it looks like the  real deal  from the stained-glass windows gargoyles  and the towers the animated version is  almost indistinguishable from the real  Cathedral the filmmakers studied the  inside of the Cathedral and