ars lieutenant-colonel John McCrae  Gilstrap bought the island in 1911 and  spent 20 years rebuilding Elendil in the  castle we see today is the same  structure that was finished in 1932 the  second castle is done at our castle it's  it's spread across the top of a flat top  island surrounded by the North Sea the  natural pathways were destroyed to  prevent attacks but instead a new path  was cut into the cliffs we can totally  see why these two castles were used for  dunbroch the view around them is  absolutely mad  chuckle tangled mont saint-michel  disney's 2010 movie Tangled was a  magical and hairy adventure Rapunzel's  story began much the same as the  original fairy tale but was a twist this  Rapunzel was much sassier and had a pet  and bestfriend chameleon named Pascal  she was locked away in a beautiful tower  until a runaway thief Flynn Rider came  into the picture she was then able to  find out who she really was a princess  her world was set in the kingdom of  Corona which is a gorgeous island  surrounded by water Corona was inspired  by Mont saint-michel in Normandy France  the island was invaded by some of the  highest tides in Europe which means that  it was sometimes cut off from the  mainland as waters rise the first  structure on this island happened during  the 8th century whose structures served  as a monastery and was named after the  Archangel Michael the structure  temporary was turned into a prison but  closed in 1836 it was later declared  that Mont saint-michel is a historic  monument the bait was also protected as  it has been added to a list of world  heritage sites this island was  definitely worth a visit don't you think  just don't get stranded with rising  tides cars shamrock Texas Lightning  McQueen sped on two screens and the hit  movie cars although we usually think of  princesses and extravagant castles cars  provided a breath of fresh air  aside from featuring non-human  characters cars also featured very  realistic-looking locations in cars  except for the eyeballs in the talkie of  course lightning story began on the race  track as a celebrity but when he entered  the town of Radiator Springs on route 66  it started looking even more real and  for a good reason one of the shops in  the film was a real-life location  Ramon's house of body art in the film  was based on the you droppin in shamrock  Texas in 1930 highway 83 and the famous  route 66 were completed up through  shamrock Texas you drop in was built  around it in 1936 much like many shops  the building was built by JN Tyndall and  RC Lewis and costs twenty-three thousand  dollars the design represented the  popular art deco style of the 20s and  30s the building closed down when roots  t6 was decommissioned but was renovated  in 2003 thanks to a 1.7 million dollar  grant now it is a museum visitor center  and even a Tesla electric car charging  station we about lightning is a big fan  of the upgrades Beauty and the Beast  chateau de chambord love is a tale as  old as time wouldn't you say  Belen beasts love story is that of a  fantastic fairy tale the 1991 film was  full of magic including talking objects  dancing a prince and you guessed it a  castle such a beautiful castle had to  take inspiration from somewhere equally  fantastic right well the real-life  inspiration for beasts a que Prince  Adams castle was the chateau de chambord  the shampo is located in the Loire  Valley surrounded by woods  sounds a bit familiar the counts of blue  ah had originally created a palace as a  place to be used for hunting in 1518  Francis the first demolished it and  built a massive mansion the Shambaugh  has four hundred rooms 80 staircases 365  fireplaces and is full of gorgeous high  ceilings the interior is the epitome of  royal and we can definitely see where a  disney got their inspiration from the  ornate walls paintings and tapestries  scream regal now if being in here does  it make you feel like a princess we  don't know what will the 